      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- CIS_COURSE_CATALOG\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\n\n## Column Mapping\n- subjects offered in the academic year 2024: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- CIS course catalog: CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.SUBJECT_ID\n- Mathematics department: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- Course 18: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- subject ID: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- subject code: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_CODE, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE\n- subject number: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_NUMBER\n- department name: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- subject short title: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_SHORT_TITLE\n- subject title: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- lecture units: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.LECTURE_UNITS\n- lab units: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.LAB_UNITS\n- total units: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n- grade type: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.GRADE_TYPE\n- grade rule: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.GRADE_RULE\n- minimum total units value over each department code group: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- geometric mean of the total units for subjects offered by that department: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- subjects offered this year: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR\n- total units greater than zero: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n\n## Join Keys\n- CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.SUBJECT_ID <-> COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_CODE <-> SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"math\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n- \"Course 18\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 that are also present in the CIS course catalog and are in the Mathematics department (Course 18), show the subject ID, subject code, subject number, department name, subject short title, subject title, lecture units, lab units, total units, grade type, grade rule, and the minimum total units value over each department code group, ordered by department code.\n```sql\nSELECT t0.SUBJECT_ID, t0.SUBJECT_CODE, t0.SUBJECT_NUMBER, t0.DEPARTMENT_NAME, t0.SUBJECT_SHORT_TITLE, t0.SUBJECT_TITLE, t0.LECTURE_UNITS, t0.LAB_UNITS, t0.TOTAL_UNITS, t0.GRADE_TYPE, t0.GRADE_RULE, min(t0.TOTAL_UNITS) OVER (PARTITION BY t0.DEPARTMENT_CODE ORDER BY t0.DEPARTMENT_CODE) AS min_total_units_by_dept FROM COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED t0 JOIN CIS_COURSE_CATALOG t1 ON t0.SUBJECT_ID = t1.SUBJECT_ID WHERE t0.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2024 AND t0.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' ORDER BY t0.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n```\n2. For each department, what is the department name and the geometric mean of the total units for subjects offered by that department, considering only subjects that are offered this year, have total units greater than zero, and are in the Mathematics department (Course 18)?\n```sql\nSELECT scd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, EXP(AVG(LN(ccso.TOTAL_UNITS))) AS geometric_mean_total_units FROM SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION scd JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ccso ON scd.COURSE = ccso.SUBJECT_CODE WHERE ccso.IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR = 'Y' AND ccso.TOTAL_UNITS > 0 AND scd.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' AND scd.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' GROUP BY scd.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY geometric_mean_total_units DESC;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor subjects offered in the academic year 2024 that are also present in the CIS course catalog and are in the Mathematics department (Course 18), show the subject ID, subject code, subject number, department name, subject short title, subject title, lecture units, lab units, total units, grade type, grade rule, the minimum total units value over each department code group, and the geometric mean of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects that are offered this year, have total units greater than zero, and are in the Mathematics department), ordered by department name and subject code. Do not return any rounded answers."
